# Open Library
Books by what they're called, who wrote them, and their covers.
Every thing it shows is in OpenLibrary.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it;  each type below adds to its type there,
with `<extend>`, so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.
Open Library has no list of every book, only a search:  so the page always searches, for what's typed.

<thing "open library page">
	<spell>
		- its "search" is text
		- its "showing" is a book
		- to create it:
			set its search to "dune"
	</spell>
	<property "found" description="What the search finds:  Open Library looks, by the title, and gives back the first hundred">every book where its title includes the search</property>

	<draw>
		<stack spacing="xl">
			<form value={it}>
				<stack direction="horizontal" wrap align="center" justify="between" spacing="sm">
					<header size="large">Books, from Open Library</header>
					<ui-search name="search" parameter="book" icon="search" placeholder="A book, by its title" aria-label="Search Open Library" />
				</stack>
			</form>
			{draw the shelf of it}
			<text size="small" paragraph>
				From <link link="https://openlibrary.org/developers/api">Open Library's API</link>, asked for as you look;  its covers from its covers server.
			</text>
		</stack>
	</draw>

	<draw "shelf" description="A book's own page, while one is open;  else what the search finds">
		<if its showing>
			draw its showing's page
		<otherwise>
			draw the book list of it
		</>
	</draw>

	<draw "book list">
		<for its found as="cards" columns="5" doubling paging="pages" loading="Asking Open Library" failed="Open Library can't be reached just now." empty="No book is called that." />
	</draw>
</thing>


# A book
Its cover, its title and who wrote it:  on its card, every name the search gave;  on its own page, its first author, read from their own record.

<extend "book">
	<property "writer" description="Who wrote it first:  read from Open Library's record of them, by their id">the first item of its authors</property>

	<draw>
		<ui-card class="book" onClick={open it}>
			<image src={its cover i} alt="" aspect-ratio="2:3" crop />
			<content>
				<header>{its title}</header>
				<meta>{its author name} · {its first publish year}</meta>
			</content>
		</ui-card>
	</draw>

	<draw "page">
		<stack spacing="xl">
			<stack direction="horizontal" align="center" spacing="sm">
				<button icon="arrow left" appearance="basic" aria-label="Back" title="Back" onClick={close it} />
				<header size="large">{its title}</header>
			</stack>
			<stack direction="horizontal" wrap align="start" spacing="md">
				<image src={its cover i} alt="" size="small" />
				<stack spacing="sm">
					<text>First published in {its first publish year} · {its edition count} editions</text>
					{draw the writing of it}
				</stack>
			</stack>
		</stack>
	</draw>

	<draw "writing">
		<if its writer>
			draw the card of its writer
		</if>
		while waiting:
			<loader visible inline text>Asking Open Library who wrote it</loader>
		if that fails:
			<text>Open Library can't say who wrote it just now.</text>
	</draw>
</extend>


# Who wrote it

<extend "author">
	<draw "card">
		<ui-card>
			<content>
				<header>{its name}</header>
				<meta>Born {its birth date}</meta>
				<description>{its bio}</description>
			</content>
		</ui-card>
	</draw>
</extend>
